# Discord Dice UI - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
React + TypeScript dice rolling app for tabletop RPGs with Discord integration. Uses Redux for state management, extensive middleware pattern for roll processing.

## Code Style

### TypeScript
- Use strict type checking
- Avoid `any` types - add proper interfaces/types
- Use explicit return types for functions
- Interface for component props, type for action payloads

### React
- Functional components with hooks only
- Props interface: `interface ComponentNameProps { ... }`
- Keep components under 200 lines
- Extract complex logic to custom hooks or utilities

### Redux
- Action types as string constants
- Action creators in `actions/` directory
- Pure reducers in `reducers/` directory
- Side effects only in middleware
- Immutable state updates

### File Organization
- One component per file
- Colocate styles if component-specific
- Group by feature/system, not by type
- Index files for easy imports

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`DiceModule.tsx`)
- Actions: kebab-case + `.actions.ts` (`conan.actions.ts`)
- Reducers: kebab-case + `-reducer.ts` (`conan-reducer.ts`)
- Middleware: kebab-case + `.middleware.ts` (`handleRoll.middleware.ts`)
- Utils: camelCase (`getDiceSet.ts`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for values, camelCase for files

## Patterns to Follow

### Middleware Pattern
```typescript
const myMiddleware = (store: any) => (next: any) => (action: any) => {
  if (action.type === MY_ACTION_TYPE) {
    // Handle action
  }
  return next(action);
};
export default myMiddleware;
```

### Action Creator Pattern
```typescript
export const ACTION_TYPE = 'FEATURE_ACTION_TYPE';
export interface ActionPayload { /* ... */ }
export function actionCreator(payload: ActionPayload) {
  return { type: ACTION_TYPE, payload };
}
```

### Component Pattern
```typescript
interface MyComponentProps {
  prop1: string;
  prop2?: number;
}

const MyComponent: React.FC<MyComponentProps> = ({ prop1, prop2 }) => {
  // Component logic
  return <div>{/* JSX */}</div>;
};
export default MyComponent;
```

## Important Rules

1. **Never use Math.random()** - Use `random-js` library for dice rolls
2. **Two message types** - Local (HTML/JSX) for app, Request (plain text) for Discord
3. **Add middleware to store.ts** - Don't forget to register in middleware array
4. **Immutable state** - Always return new objects in reducers
5. **Bootstrap 4 components** - Use react-bootstrap, not custom CSS when possible
6. **Type the state** - Redux state should have proper TypeScript types
7. **Mode-based rendering** - Check mode before rendering system-specific UI
8. **Query params** - Support configuration via URL parameters
9. **Local storage** - Persist user preferences and character sheets
10. **Accessibility** - Use semantic HTML and ARIA labels

## When Adding Features

### New Game System Checklist
- [ ] Action file in `src/actions/`
- [ ] Reducer in `src/reducers/` and add to `index.ts`
- [ ] Middleware for roll processing
- [ ] Middleware for message generation (local + request)
- [ ] Register middleware in `src/store.ts`
- [ ] Modal component for input
- [ ] Results modal component
- [ ] Add mode to `DiceModuleOptions/store.ts`
- [ ] Update `App.tsx` for mode routing
- [ ] Add dice constants if needed
- [ ] Add to README.md documentation

### New Component Checklist
- [ ] Props interface with proper types
- [ ] Use React Bootstrap components
- [ ] Responsive design (mobile-friendly)
- [ ] Proper accessibility attributes
- [ ] Error boundaries if needed
- [ ] Connect to Redux if state needed
- [ ] Export as default

## Testing Preferences
- Write tests for utility functions
- Test reducers (pure functions, easy to test)
- Integration tests for middleware chains
- Component tests for complex UI logic
- Manual testing in dev mode

## Don't
- ❌ Don't modify `node_modules`
- ❌ Don't use class components
- ❌ Don't mix concerns in components
- ❌ Don't use inline styles (use Bootstrap classes)
- ❌ Don't forget error handling
- ❌ Don't ignore TypeScript errors
- ❌ Don't use deprecated lifecycle methods
- ❌ Don't hardcode values (use constants)
- ❌ Don't bypass middleware for state changes
- ❌ Don't use global variables

## Do
- ✅ Use semantic HTML
- ✅ Follow existing file structure
- ✅ Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- ✅ Keep functions pure when possible
- ✅ Use descriptive variable names
- ✅ Handle loading and error states
- ✅ Make UI responsive
- ✅ Support keyboard navigation
- ✅ Test in multiple browsers
- ✅ Update documentation when needed
